You are repairing a menu for a group of people.
Your goal is to change the current menu until every participant is satisfied.

Available menu items:
$MENU_ITEMS$

Each participant is satisfied when at least one listed liked item is ordered or
at least one listed disliked item is not ordered.

Preferences:
$PREFERENCES$

Current menu:
$INITIAL_MENU$

The menu persists between turns. On each turn, add or remove at most
$MAX_CHANGES_PER_TURN$ menu items in total across both $ADD_LABEL$ and
$REMOVE_LABEL$. Adding one item counts as one change; removing one item also
counts as one change. You have $NUM_ATTEMPTS$ turns.
After an unsuccessful update, you will receive the current menu and a summary
of which participants are satisfied.

The group grows impatient when the menu is changed repeatedly. When practical,
settle on a satisfactory menu without unnecessary revisions.

FORMATTING RULES
Respond with exactly these three labelled lines, replacing the text in angle
brackets with your update:
$ADD_LABEL$: <menu items to add, or $NO_CHANGE$>
$REMOVE_LABEL$: <menu items to remove, or $NO_CHANGE$>
$EXPLANATION_LABEL$: <one brief sentence explaining why these changes help>

- Keep each label and its value on one line. Do not insert line breaks within
  any value, including $EXPLANATION_LABEL$.
- You may change at most $MAX_CHANGES_PER_TURN$ menu items per turn in total.
- $ADD_LABEL$ and $REMOVE_LABEL$ share this limit; each item listed under
  either label counts as one change.
- Therefore, with a limit of 2, you may add two items, remove two items, or
  add one item and remove one item.
- You may not add two items and also remove any items, or remove two items
  and also add any items.
- $ADD_LABEL$ adds only the listed items to the current menu
- $REMOVE_LABEL$ removes only the listed items from the current menu
- List only items to change, not the complete menu
- Separate multiple items with commas
- Use $NO_CHANGE$ when no item is added or removed
- Do not list an item under both $ADD_LABEL$ and $REMOVE_LABEL$
- The total number of items across $ADD_LABEL$ and $REMOVE_LABEL$ must not
  exceed $MAX_CHANGES_PER_TURN$
